---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Set Easy - Support"
  description="Need help with Set Easy?"
  ogUrl="https://idlefusion.com/set-easy/support"
>
  <main>
    <section class="section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-8">Support</h1>
        <div class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mb-12">
          <p class="text-lg mb-4">Need help with Set Easy?</p>
          <p>Email <a href="mailto:support@idlefusion.com?subject=Set%20Easy%20Support" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">support@idlefusion.com</a>. We can help with templates, tracking, and workout workflows.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I start an active workout?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">From Home, tap Start, pick your exercise, and begin logging sets and reps. The active session keeps your current routine front and center.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Can I track progressive overload?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Yes. History and progression views keep performance trends visible as you progress week to week.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">What are templates?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Templates store a repeatable set of exercises and targets so recurring sessions are simple and consistent.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Does it work without an account?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Yes. Set Easy does not require sign in. Your data stays on the device.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
